story += [pair('dayrally-mini-flow','dayrally-mini-drop'),fig('dayrally-mini-ridge',300),table([['Model','Direction','Geometry'],['FLOW','Park / playful','Compact fixed-frame silhouette, equal-size wheels, single-crown fork.'],['DROP','Downhill','Longer stance, larger wheels and twin-crown fork geometry.'],['RIDGE','Enduro','Distinct frame geometry with a larger front wheel.']],[75,90,330]),p('These are display-scale miniatures. They are not rideable bicycles or licensed replicas, and their proportions are original rather than manufacturer dimensions. No child-toy testing was carried out.','SmallAC')]
page();head(9,'mini bike assembly & personalisation.')
story += [p('Each assembled miniature uses 13 component instances. Some wheel/axle components are shared across models; the frame, fork, cockpit, saddle, cranks and named base are model-specific.'),table([['Stage','Action / check'],['1. Prepare','Print the selected frame, fork and wheels with support review. Clear the narrow bores without enlarging them arbitrarily.'],['2. Fork','Insert the steerer through the head-tube bore. Seat the cockpit on the steerer. Retention must be proven in a sample.'],['3. Saddle','Slide the square socket over the post. Do not force a poor fit.'],['4. Cranks','Install the shaft-bearing crank through the bottom bracket, then the separate socket crank on the opposite side.'],['5. Wheels','Place each wheel between its outboard supports. Insert one axle and one cap. Check free clearance and cap retention.'],['6. Base','Rest the wheels in the shallow base pockets. The base is a display support, not a permanent fixing.']],[85,410]),p('What moves, and what does not','H2AC'),p('Wheel and steerer bores have nominal clearance. No physical rolling test, steering-range test or retention test was performed. The frame and shock detail are fixed. There is no functioning suspension, chain drive or miniature gear mechanism.'),p('Real custom-name rebuild','H2AC'),p('Run <font face="BodyBold">python source/build_all.py --group bikes --name MILA --out ./mila-mini-bikes</font> in a suitable CAD development environment. A fresh output folder protects the supplied revision. The name is cut into the native base solid, not painted onto a texture.'),p('The sample rebuild changed the JACK bases to MILA while keeping the outer dimensions unchanged. Production interfaces must remain locked when connecting this to the storefront.'),p('Do not globally scale a miniature to fit another kit: the shaft and socket gaps would scale too. Regenerate the specific design and inspect the changed geometry.')]
